## Lore

Auto-Gs are a rare and much-feared D-Bee that call themselves human and
look exactly like humans in their own form. They are shape-changers of a
unique kind: by eating a scrap of another being''s DNA they rebuild their
own bodies, genes and all, into a member of that race, gaining its
abilities along with its looks. Given time to study a particular person and
a larger sample, an Auto-G can become that person''s perfect double, down to
fingerprints and blood tests. Only its memories, habits and skills stay its
own, and a careful impostor learns to copy those too.

That talent makes them superb spies, infiltrators and assassins, and the
perfect tool for framing the innocent, so nearly everyone who believes in
them wants them dead. Most people think they are a Dark Age bogeyman. The
Coalition knows better: it has hunted them since the early days of
Chi-Town, tests suspects for a telltale enzyme, and in 106 P.A. foiled a
plot by an Auto-G assassin to replace a member of the Prosek family. Their
numbers in North America are guessed at a few hundred at most.

Persecution has left most Auto-Gs cold, bitter or angry toward the humans
they insist they belong among, and many are bold, cocky and self-assured.

## GM Notes

Size and weight: human in natural form, otherwise as the race copied. Life
span 6D6+134 years. Experience Level for NPCs: 1D8.

Habitat: anywhere, hidden among humans and D-Bees; possibly from the
Devil''s Gate at St. Louis or a Rift in the ruins of old Chicago. Fewer than
600 believed to live in North America, perhaps as few as 200.

Slave Market Value: 1D6x100,000 credits.

Allies: only their own kind; criminals keep criminal company. Some are said
to work with the Federation of Magic, and Tolkeen hired Auto-G assassins
and spies. Enemies: almost everyone who discovers one, the Coalition first
of all; Splugorth Slavers trade in them.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'auto-g');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'auto-g';

